  <TR class=3DNoteAlso>
    <TD class=3DNoteAlso><A name=3D1005775></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><STRONG class=3DNH>See=20
      Also:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D1005782></A>
      <P class=3DNB><A=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/optimops.htm#39473">"Understanding=20
      Joins"</A><A=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/optimops.htm#39473"></A></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A=20
name=3D1005784></A><!--TOC=3Dh4-"1005784"-->
<H5 class=3DH4><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Complex=20
View Merging</FONT></H5><!--/TOC=3Dh4--><A name=3D1005793></A>
<P class=3DBP>If a view's query contains a <CODE>GROUP</CODE> =
<CODE>BY</CODE>=20
clause or <CODE>DISTINCT</CODE> operator in the select list, then the =
optimizer=20
can merge the view's query into the accessing statement only if complex =
view=20
merging is enabled. Complex merging of a view with a <CODE>GROUP</CODE>=20
<CODE>BY</CODE> clause is illustrated in <A=20
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/opt_ops.htm#1005820">Example&nbsp;2-43</A>.</P><A=20
name=3D1010592></A>
<P class=3DBP>Complex merging can also be used to merge an =
<CODE>IN</CODE>=20
subquery into the accessing statement if the subquery is uncorrelated, =
as shown=20
in <A=20
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/opt_ops.htm#1005841">Example&nbsp;2-44</A>.=20
Complex merging is not cost-based; it must be enabled with the =
initialization=20
parameter <CODE>OPTIMIZER_FEATURES_ENABLE</CODE> or the =
<CODE>MERGE</CODE> hint.=20
Without this hint or parameter setting, the optimizer uses another =
approach,=20
pushing predicates.</P><A name=3D1005819></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
